 and tricks but was ultimately surpassed by her teammate Yoshizawa’s exceptional performance."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141168"} "Rayssa Leal"] ", the Tokyo 2020 silver medalist, finished with the bronze medal, with her score of 253.37 points. At 16, Leal became the youngest person to reach the Olympic podium in two different Games, surpassing a record held since 1932. Her final trick, a kickflip Smith grind, secured her place on the podium amidst a crowd filled with enthusiastic Brazilian fans."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144430"} "Funa Nakayama"] ", the bronze medalist from Tokyo 2020, finished seventh after struggling to land her tricks."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/154277"} "Coco Yoshizawa"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "258.92 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "272.75 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/154279"} "Liz Akama"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "257.99 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "265.95 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141168"} "Rayssa Leal"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BRA.png"}] "BRA"]] [:td {} "241.43 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "253.37 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronz